{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531931-advice-on-porting-an-idea-from-w-tf","id":1531931,"title":"Advice on porting an idea from W:TF","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-03T16:23:01-08:00","id":1531931,"title":"Advice on porting an idea from W:TF","content":"I once had an antagonist idea for W: TF, and I had the idea of transferring it to the W: TA universe. I want some thoughts on how to do it.<br /> <br /> (Some mood music <a href=\"https://youtu.be/xycRCykPv2w?si=i2lul2DIcRw1Rq-C\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/xycRCykPv2w?si=i2lul2DIcRw1Rq-C</a>)<br /> <br /> The Hawthorne Principle is a Scientology-like cult that sprung up in the 60s or 70s. It was founded by Phillip Hawthorne, a renowned archeologist and amateur Theologian after he returned from a &quot;Enlightening&quot; excursion from a unknown corner of the Earth. The Cult itself seems very good at attracting converts, especially celebrities. It appears to have almost no controversy surrounding it, but it is still quick to shut down any investigation or news story about them, especially when it concerns their VIP members.<br /> <br /> My idea centers around them being a cult that somehow centered their theology on reverence to The Garou, heavy research into The Umbra via laboratories hidden across the globe, and worship to a bitter progeny of a powerful tribal totem that wanted its own tribe and somehow focused his attention to Hawthorne and now uses the Cult to try and lure Garou away to join with them.<br /> <br /> This is still a basic idea, and I would appreciate any advice on further fleshing it out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","